WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.868
Before the size of the job, it
helps to know which job is whose,

2
00:00:03.868 --> 00:00:07.375
because one O U tree holds
four different populations.

3
00:00:07.375 --> 00:00:10.100
The workbook treats them as four tracks.

4
00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:14.292
People, the HR track: this book
builds the directory side,

5
00:00:14.292 --> 00:00:17.938
and HR-Driven Identity
supplies the attributes.

6
00:00:17.938 --> 00:00:22.550
End-user devices and servers, the Intune
and Arc tracks: this book's Group

7
00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:27.475
Policy analysis finds their settings,
and Devices and Endpoints moves them.

8
00:00:27.475 --> 00:00:32.364
And the non-person track: every service
account gets an owner and a target,

9
00:00:32.364 --> 00:00:36.275
here in this book, with AI agents
in AI Identity Governance.

10
00:00:36.275 --> 00:00:39.706
Appendix A maps that work
to account management,

11
00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:45.625
attribute-based access and least
privilege in NIST 800-53, and to M-22-09.

12
00:00:45.625 --> 00:00:48.530
Next, everything else
the directory holds up.
